The legal texts come from the LEGI database of the Direction de l'information légale et administrative (DILA),
published on Légifrance and as open data:

  Source : DILA, Légifrance, base LEGI (www.legifrance.gouv.fr),
  https://echanges.dila.gouv.fr/OPENDATA/LEGI/, retrieved 28 October 2026
  (full dump of 13 July 2025 and every daily update to LEGI_20261028-212713).

They are reused under the Licence Ouverte / Open Licence version 2.0 (Etalab):
https://www.etalab.gouv.fr/licence-ouverte-open-licence

Changes made by Lexifina: each article version was converted to one Markdown file per article, one paragraph per
line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised and markup removed; LEGI's editorial notes (NOTA) were left out;
the article versions in force on each day were arranged as git commits, credited to the texts LEGI's own amendment
links name. The wording of the law was not changed. DILA does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
